# The store listing lives in App Store Connect and not here. Everything asc keeps on
# disk is either a working file for one command or a local copy of what the store
# already holds, and both are shaped by that one store: keywords cut to its hundred
# characters, screenshots named by its display types. This repository is the base a
# build for any platform comes off, so a store's own schema does not belong in it.
# `asc metadata pull` fetches the listing whenever it is wanted, which is what makes
# the copy a derivative rather than the original.
.asc/
/metadata/
/screenshots/

# Profiler captures. One is 65MB of a few seconds of frames on one device, taken to
# answer one question; what it is worth keeping is the number it settled, which belongs
# in the comment that argues for the code it is about. The directory is a workbench, so
# it stays out of the history and the captures stay to hand.
/ProfilerCaptures/

# Plan files. `plansDirectory` puts them beside the code they are about rather than in
# ~/.claude, where a plan for this repository is filed under a path nothing here can
# see. They are a working note for one change, superseded by the commit that carries it
# out and by the comment that argues for it, so the directory is to hand and out of the
# history.
/plans/
